# What to include in the npm tarball (`npm pack`).
# Everything else in the source tree is excluded automatically.
# This file is the SOURCE OF TRUTH for npm packaging; the
# `files` field in package.json further restricts to the
# minimum set below.
#
# We deliberately publish only what npm needs at install time.
# The Python wheel is downloaded by postinstall.js, not bundled
# into the npm tarball — that would bloat it to 70 KB+ per
# release.

# Exclude the Chinese README — npm users are the English audience.
README.zh-CN.md

# Exclude all scripts/*.py hand-run helpers (smoke / recall /
# debug / compare). Only postinstall.js and preuninstall.js
# are needed at install time, and those are explicitly listed
# in `files` above.
scripts/compare_tokenizers.py
scripts/debug_rank.py
scripts/recall_phase1.py
scripts/recall_phase2.py
scripts/smoke_bm25.py
scripts/smoke_db.py
scripts/smoke_index.py
scripts/README.md

# Exclude docs, tests, and the Python source tree.
docs/
tests/
example_wiki/
assets/
skills/
lorewiki/
*.md
!README.md
!README.npm.md
!LICENSE

# Build artifacts.
.venv/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# OS / editor noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
